Subject: wasix: expose the body of task_wasm

`TokioTaskManager::task_wasm` runs a guest thread on its pool: it
instantiates the module for the new thread, answers the spawning
syscall, runs the trigger if there is one and then the task. That body
is now `run_task_wasm`, callable on any thread, so a task manager that
owns its guest threads (one OS thread each, driving a suspendable
coroutine) can reuse it. The pool path is unchanged.

